Source
World Health Organization — Patient Safety
This is an authoritative healthcare source, not a research paper.
What it covers
WHO describes patient safety as a fundamental part of healthcare quality.
The source highlights harm that can occur because of unsafe healthcare processes and includes areas such as:
Medication errors
Diagnostic errors
Healthcare-associated infections
Falls
Patient identification problems
Other preventable adverse events
WHO states that approximately 1 in 10 patients is harmed in healthcare, making patient safety a strong justification for systems intended to improve monitoring and response.
CAREGRID connection
CAREGRID is designed around operational safety events including:
Bed-exit events
IV-low events
Fall/SOS events
Nurse-call events
Emergency response
Design decision
CAREGRID is designed as a monitoring and coordination system rather than an autonomous treatment system.
Why this matters
The safety source supports the problem motivation, but it does not validate CAREGRID's technology.
Your research chain should be:
